## Permitted Purposes

Use of the software is use for a permitted purpose if it falls under any of the following sections.

### Personal Uses

Use by an individual for research, experiment, testing, learning, hobby projects or other personal purposes is use for a
permitted purpose, as long as the use does not benefit any organization that does not itself qualify under
[Small Business](#small-business).

### Small Business

Use of the software for the benefit of your company is use for a permitted purpose if your company has no more than 10
employees and had less than 5,000,000 USD revenue in its last completed fiscal year (or, in its first fiscal year,
expects less than that in the current one).

**Employees** are counted as full-time equivalents averaged over the last 12 months (a part-time worker counts
proportionally), including working owners, independent contractors and agency staff who work for your company at least
20 hours a week on average. **Revenue** means the consolidated gross revenue of your company. Both figures always cover
your company as defined below, including every organization that controls it, is controlled by it, or is under common
control with it. Revenue in another currency is converted to USD at the average European Central Bank reference rates
for that fiscal year.

This section does not cover use for the benefit of any other organization that is not itself a qualifying company under
this section, including operating, hosting or providing the software, or its output, as a service to such an
organization.

If your company stops meeting these limits, this section continues to apply to your company's use of the software until
the earlier of (a) 90 days after the end of the month (employees) or of the fiscal year (revenue) in which a limit was
first exceeded and (b) the day a commercial license starts.

### Evaluation

Use of the software by any company for internal evaluation, to decide whether to take a commercial license, is use for a
permitted purpose for 30 days from the first use by any person for that company. This applies once per company (including
every organization that is part of it under [Definitions](#definitions)) unless the licensor agrees in writing to an
extension. Evaluation does not cover use in production or for
the benefit of the company's customers.

### REAX Subnet

Use of the software by anyone, of any size, is use for a permitted purpose to the extent the use is for taking part in
the REAX subnet, and only for that purpose. The **REAX subnet** is the subnet with netuid 92 on the Bittensor main
network while the licensor or an organization the licensor designates operates it, together with its test networks and
any successor subnet the licensor designates in writing or in the README of this repository. This covers:

1. running a miner or a validator for the REAX subnet, including serving inference requests that reach your miner
   through the REAX subnet from its validators or from the REAX subnet's official gateway;
2. building, testing, measuring and submitting engines or other entries to competitions of the REAX subnet, including
   changing the software and building container images from it for that purpose; and
3. publishing the source code and container images of such entries as the REAX subnet's rules require or allow.

Serving requests that reach you any other way, using the same deployment for your own customers or products, or using
the software or changes and new works based on it outside the REAX subnet is not covered by this section.

Use that was permitted under this section when it took place stays permitted. If the REAX subnet ends, entries already
submitted and published may continue to be used and distributed for the purposes in items 1 to 3 for 12 months.

If you submit an entry based on the software to a competition of the REAX subnet, you grant the licensor a perpetual,
irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free, sublicensable copyright and patent license to use, change, distribute and license,
including under these terms and under commercial licenses, your changes and new works contained in that entry. You
confirm that you have the right to grant this license. Third-party components in the entry stay under their own licenses
and are not covered by this grant.

## Commercial Licenses

Any use that is not a permitted purpose needs a separate written commercial license from the licensor. Contact the
licensor at info@decisionmodels.io. As a non-binding guide, a commercial license currently costs about:

- USD 1,000 per year for a company with more than 10 employees or at least 5,000,000 USD annual revenue; and
- USD 10,000 per year for a company with at least 1,000 employees or at least 500,000,000 USD annual revenue,

counted as in [Small Business](#small-business), plus VAT where applicable. These figures are not an offer and may change.
Only a signed commercial license agreement grants rights beyond these terms, apart from written extensions under
[Evaluation](#evaluation) and designations under [REAX Subnet](#reax-subnet). On request, you must tell the licensor in
good faith whether your company meets the limits in [Small Business](#small-business).

